From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:44:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/UsbBusDxe: Guard descriptor on SS retry

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0047, as it is]

UsbEnumerateNewDev() frees DevDesc before resetting the port for an
enumeration retry. UsbRootHubResetPort() scans that device during the
reset and previously dereferenced DevDesc without checking it.

For a SuperSpeed-capable device running below SuperSpeed, IsSSDev and
Speed still satisfy the scan's preceding conditions after DevDesc is
cleared. The DeviceClass access can therefore cause a null-pointer
exception. Add descriptor checks before those dereferences and clear
IsSSDev when freeing the descriptor.

The unsafe reset dereference was introduced by PR #12714:
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/pull/12714

Signed-off-by: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit 7250fc9e3941 (merged on
2026-10-21, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: PR #12714 (4d5f8e68a1e9, "MdeModulePkg/UsbBusDxe: BOS
Descriptor Check for SS Devices") is in the base. A SuperSpeed-capable
device that comes up below SuperSpeed on a root port of the xHCI
controller of either board (a USB 2 cable, a link that does not train)
takes that retry, and UsbRootHubResetPort() then read the device class
through the descriptor that UsbEnumerateNewDev() had freed and set to
NULL. The payload has no NULL pointer detection
(PcdNullPointerDetectionPropertyMask is 0), so the read went to low
memory instead of faulting; its byte only decided whether the reset of
the port waited longer.

TEST=git am on the series: clean, at other offsets (MrChromebox's
UsbEnumer.c and UsbHub.c move them), the same lines as upstream. No
test with such a device.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbEnumer.c | 2 ++
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbHub.c    | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbEnumer.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbEnumer.c
index 64da8d7bf..8808b9b99 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbEnumer.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbEnumer.c
@@ -862,6 +862,7 @@ DeviceRetry:
      && (Bus->Usb2Hc->MajorRevision >= 0x3)
      && (Child->IsSSDev)
      && (Child->Speed < EFI_USB_SPEED_SUPER)
+     && (Child->DevDesc != NULL)
      && (Child->DevDesc->Desc.DeviceClass != USB_HUB_CLASS_CODE))
   {
     goto ON_ERROR;
@@ -918,6 +919,7 @@ ON_ERROR:
     if ((Child != NULL) && (Child->DevDesc != NULL)) {
       UsbFreeDevDesc (Child->DevDesc);
       Child->DevDesc = NULL;
+      Child->IsSSDev = FALSE;
     }
 
     Status = HubApi->ResetPort (HubIf, Port);
diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbHub.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbHub.c
index a647ef2cf..8df914070 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbHub.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbHub.c
@@ -1180,10 +1180,15 @@ UsbRootHubResetPort (
        && (Bus->Devices[Index]->ParentPort == Port)
        && (Bus->Devices[Index]->ParentIf == RootIf))
     {
+      //
+      // DevDesc is freed and set to NULL by UsbEnumerateNewDev() before
+      // it retries the port reset, so check it before dereferencing.
+      //
       if (  (Bus->Usb2Hc != NULL)
          && (Bus->Usb2Hc->MajorRevision >= 0x3)
          && (Bus->Devices[Index]->IsSSDev)
          && (Bus->Devices[Index]->Speed < EFI_USB_SPEED_SUPER)
+         && (Bus->Devices[Index]->DevDesc != NULL)
          && (Bus->Devices[Index]->DevDesc->Desc.DeviceClass != USB_HUB_CLASS_CODE))
       {
         DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "Found the device matched, Index = %d, Port = %X, ParentIf = %X\n", Index, Port, RootIf));
-- 
